  <h1>Raina Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Privacy Agreement<br>Effective date: July 16, 2026</p>

  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how the provider of the Raina mobile application identified on Raina’s App Store product page (“Raina,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) handles information when you use Raina. It applies to account registration, profiles, posts, images, voice recordings, comments, messages, virtual coins and unlocks, reports, blocking, and account-management features.</p>
  <div class="notice"><strong>Raina does not sell personal information. The current version does not include third-party advertising, cross-app tracking, or third-party analytics SDKs.</strong></div>

  <h2>1. Information you provide</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account information:</strong> email address and password. The password is stored using Apple Keychain services and is used to authenticate your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Profile information:</strong> nickname, avatar, age, and location or address text that you choose to provide.</li>
    <li><strong>Published content:</strong> post titles, descriptions, selected images, optional voice recordings, comments, and related engagement.</li>
    <li><strong>Communications:</strong> direct messages exchanged through Raina and message status needed to enforce first-contact messaging controls.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety information:</strong> reports, selected report reasons, optional report details, and the accounts you block or remove from your blacklist.</li>
    <li><strong>Feature records:</strong> virtual coin balance, content unlocks, and your published-post records.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Photos and microphone permissions</h2>
  <p>When you choose an avatar or post image, Apple’s photo picker allows you to select the specific media you want to provide. Raina receives only the items you select through that picker. Raina requests microphone access only when you choose to record an optional voice introduction or explanation for a post. You can deny or later revoke microphone permission in iOS Settings; doing so prevents new voice recording but does not prevent use of other features.</p>

  <h2>3. How information is collected</h2>
  <p>We collect information directly from your entries and selections, from actions you take within Raina, and from records necessary to provide account, messaging, moderation, coin, and unlock features. The current version primarily stores these records locally on your device using protected application storage, Apple Keychain, and the application’s Documents directory. Information may also be included in device backups according to your Apple and iOS backup settings.</p>

  <h2>4. How information is used</h2>
  <p>We use information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>create and authenticate accounts;</li>
    <li>display and update profiles;</li>
    <li>publish posts and play selected image or voice content;</li>
    <li>provide comments, messages, first-contact limits, coin balances, and content unlocks;</li>
    <li>process reports, apply blocks, hide blocked users’ posts, and protect the community;</li>
    <li>maintain security, diagnose errors, prevent abuse, and enforce the User Agreement;</li>
    <li>comply with applicable law and valid legal process; and</li>
    <li>respond to support, privacy, safety, and legal requests.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Visibility and disclosure</h2>
  <p>Your nickname, avatar, posts, images, voice content, and comments may be visible to other Raina users as part of the community experience. Direct messages are intended for their participants, but recipients may retain or share what you send. Avoid publishing or messaging information you consider confidential.</p>
  <p>We may disclose information when reasonably necessary to comply with law, respond to valid legal process, protect a person’s safety, investigate fraud or abuse, enforce our agreements, or protect Raina’s rights. If service providers are engaged to support Raina in the future, they will be permitted to process information only for contracted purposes and subject to appropriate confidentiality and security obligations. If Apple In-App Purchase is offered, Apple processes transaction and payment information under Apple’s own terms and privacy policy; Raina may receive purchase status needed to deliver the digital item.</p>

  <h2>6. Storage and security</h2>
  <p>Raina uses measures appropriate to the nature of the information, including Apple Keychain for account passwords and iOS application storage protections. No storage system or security measure can guarantee absolute security. Protect your device passcode and account credentials, keep iOS current, and do not share passwords.</p>

  <h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>Information is retained for as long as needed to provide the features you use, maintain security, resolve disputes, and meet legal obligations. You can delete individual posts using the post-management controls. The in-app Delete Account feature removes the account credentials, locally stored profile, account-scoped interaction records, locally published post records, and associated locally stored avatar, image, and voice files managed by Raina on that device. Some information may remain in an iOS device backup until that backup expires or is deleted under your Apple backup settings.</p>
  <p>We may retain limited records where required by law or reasonably necessary for fraud prevention, safety, legal claims, or enforcement. When retention is no longer necessary, information is deleted or de-identified as appropriate.</p>

  <h2>8. Your controls and choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Edit your nickname, avatar, age, and location through Personal Editor.</li>
    <li>Delete your posts through My Posts.</li>
    <li>Report content or users and manage blocked users through Blacklist.</li>
    <li>Control microphone permission in iOS Settings and choose which photos to provide through Apple’s photo picker.</li>
    <li>Delete your account through the Delete Account control.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Depending on where you live, applicable law may provide additional rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to processing, or to receive a portable copy of certain information. Submit a request through the developer support contact on Raina’s App Store product page. We may need to verify your request and may retain information where legally permitted or required.</p>

  <h2>9. Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>Raina is for adults aged 18 and older and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly permit a person under 18 to register. If you believe a person under 18 has provided personal information, contact us through the developer support channel so appropriate action can be taken.</p>

  <h2>10. International use</h2>
  <p>If you use Raina outside the jurisdiction where its provider operates, privacy and data-protection rules may differ. We handle information according to this Policy and applicable law, including any mandatory protections that apply to you.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this Policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy when Raina’s features, information practices, or legal obligations change. We will update the effective date and provide additional notice when required. If a change requires consent, we will request it before applying the change as required by law.</p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>The legal provider, mailing details, and current privacy and support channel for Raina are identified through the developer information and support contact published on Raina’s App Store product page. Use that channel for privacy questions, rights requests, complaints, or account-deletion support.</p>

